
"smart_sources:2026-07-25 - Increased ‘gunk’ in Boise River led to DEQ testing. It’s ‘rock snot.’ Huh_.md": {"path":"2026-07-25 - Increased ‘gunk’ in Boise River led to DEQ testing. It’s ‘rock snot.’ Huh_.md","last_embed":{"hash":null},"embeddings":{},"last_read":{"hash":"1gzifc3","at":1785795033966},"class_name":"SmartSource","last_import":{"mtime":1785168956798,"size":8711,"at":1785795034036,"hash":"1gzifc3"},"blocks":{"#---frontmatter---":[1,9],"#":[10,35],"##The dangers and debates surrounding didymo":[36,67],"##The dangers and debates surrounding didymo#{1}":[38,67],"##The Boise River may stay like this for a while":[68,94],"##The Boise River may stay like this for a while#{1}":[70,94]},"outlinks":[{"title":"Hannah Smith","target":"Hannah Smith","line":5},{"title":"Since the first week of July, gunk has been getting caught on Chandler Bondurant’s fly-fishing gear in the Boise River, making it nearly impossible to fish near town.","target":"https://www.idahostatesman.com/public/latest-news/5yl31z/picture316628570/alternates/FREE_1200/Didymo%20algae%20detected%20in%20the%20Boise%20River","line":28,"embedded":true},{"title":"Didymo algae, or “rock snot,” found on a rock in the Boise River. Didymo is often tan or white and looks mucousy, but feels like wet wool.","target":"https://www.idahostatesman.com/public/latest-news/3jg7yo/picture316652147/alternates/FREE_1200/Didymo%20on%20rock%20in%20Boise%20River.jpg","line":42,"embedded":true},{"title":"USGS data","target":"https://nas.er.usgs.gov/queries/CollectionInfo.aspx?SpeciesID=2856&HUCNumber=5","line":52},{"title":"Didymo algae, often referred to as “rock snot” is creeping into the Boise River ecosystem.","target":"https://www.idahostatesman.com/public/latest-news/lwpaoh/picture316650485/alternates/FREE_1200/BOI_0724didymoalgae.JPG","line":58,"embedded":true}],"metadata":{"title":"Increased ‘gunk’ in Boise River led to DEQ testing. It’s ‘rock snot.’ Huh?","source":"https://www.idahostatesman.com/news/local/community/boise/article316619141.html","author":["[[Hannah Smith]]"],"published":"2026-07-25","created":"2026-07-27","description":"After multiple calls about a brown “slime” making the water unfishable, DEQ found an algae that researchers still don’t understand well."},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[]},